		{
			"listen": "prerequest",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'OCS-APIRequest', value: 'true' });",
					"// Each request names its own user. Nextcloud answers a basic-auth request with a session",
					"// cookie, and a kept cookie would make the next request run as the previous user.",
					"pm.cookies.jar().clear(pm.collectionVariables.get('base_url') || pm.variables.get('base_url'), function () {});"
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "openregister-access-links-per-subject-v1",
		"name": "OpenRegister access links managed per subject",
		"description": "# Access links managed per subject\n\nopenspec/changes/access-links-managed-per-subject task 3.1 (REQ-ABL-005): a member mints a read link over a shared view; the view's manager lists it (creator, use count, no anchor) and revokes it, after which the link answers 404. A caller who may not publish the subject gets 404 on list and revoke, and a revoke naming another subject is 404 with the link left live.\n\nUses the two non-admin users `tests/e2e/ci/seed.sh` seeds: `e2e-owner` is the manager (owns the views), `e2e-other` the member. The outsider case is the member facing the manager's private view C: listing its links, minting over it and revoking the manager's link on it all answer 404, and that link stays live. Creates its own register, schema and views and removes them.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
